    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Wer">Wer</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="392" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðonne þæt gedon sy, ðonne rære man cyninges munde, ðæt is ðæt hy ealle gemænu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> handu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> of ægðere mægðe on anum wæpne ðam semende syllan, ðæt cyninges mund stande.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="392" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> gedon sy, ðonne rære man cyniges munde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hy ealle gemænu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> handu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> of ægðere mægðe on anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wæpne ðam semende syllan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> cyniges mund stande.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="393" ed="#liebermann"/>Cum hoc factum fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Wer_4.lnote.oe.11"/>, eleuetur inter eos regis munde (id est pax), hoc est, ut omnes communi manu de utraque cognatione in uno armorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Wer_4.lnote.oe.12"/> mediatori dent, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Wer_4.lnote.oe.13"/> regis munde stet inter eos.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="393" ed="#liebermann"/>Nachdem dies vollbracht ist, werde dann Königs-Friedensschutz errichtet, d.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Wer_4.lnote.de.1"/> h. dass sie alle von beiden Sippen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Wer_4.lnote.de1.dagger"/> mit gemeinsamer Hand auf Eine Waffe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Wer_4.lnote.de.2"/> dem Schiedsrichter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Wer_4.lnote.de.3"/> geloben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Wer_4.lnote.de.4"/>, dass Königs-Friedensschutz bestehen werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">When this is done, let the king's protection then be raised, that is, that all of them from both kindreds [of the slain and of the slayer] pledge to the arbitrator with joint hands on one weapon that the king's protection shall stand.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#wormald" corresp="#wit-h">When it is done, the king's <hi rend="italic">mund</hi> is to be established, that is that all from either kin give a common pledge on a single weapon to the arbitrator that the king's <hi rend="italic">mund</hi> will stand.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="393"><ref target="clause:IIEm_7-3">II Em 7.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 7, 3</note>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator probably Wormald, The Making of English Law (named in the original spreadsheet’s sub-header rows): check; Liebermann compares II Em 7.3.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erit <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erit MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">armor <hi rend="italic">M;</hi> amor <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">armor M; amor Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">232</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht private Erklärung wie 3¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps a private explanation like 3¹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.de1.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">393</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">des Erschlagenen und des Totschlägers</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">of the slain man and of the slayer</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">232</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Waffeneid. Dänische Beispiele 16. Jhs. für Sippeneid gemeinsamer Hand auf Eine Waffe bei Totschlagsühne gibt Phillpotts <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 225</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Waffeneid. Danish examples of the 16th cent. of a kindred oath sworn with joint hand on a single weapon at the settlement of a homicide are given by Phillpotts <hi rend="italic">Kindred</hi> 225</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">232</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Schiedsgericht 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Schiedsgericht 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Wer_4.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">232</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">on hand sellan</hi>: ‘versprechen’ ist gewöhnlich, statt <hi rend="italic">hand</hi> steht hier Waffe. Toller 862 VIIIa hält keine Ergänzung nötig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">on hand sellan</hi>: ‘promise’ is usual; here ‘weapon’ stands in place of <hi rend="italic">hand</hi>. Toller 862 VIIIa considers no supplement necessary</seg></note>
      </div>
